The most common bone tumor that occurs in children is Ewing's sarcoma. Ewing's sarcoma is a high-grade, aggressive tumor that predominantly affects the long bones of the arms and legs, and it is the most common malignant bone tumor in children.

Osteosarcoma is more common in adults and less common in children. Metastatic carcinoma and multiple myeloma are not the most common bone tumors in children.

