School-based dental health care for the whole country is a notable initiative adopted by **Australia**. This system involves integrating dental services into schools, providing regular check-ups, education, and preventive care to children, thereby promoting better oral health habits from an early age.

Other options such as the USA, New Zealand, and Sweden have implemented dental health programs, but the most well-known and comprehensive school-based dental health care system is in Australia.

